## 14. Configuration & Verification (IOS Commands)

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `spanning-tree mode rapid-pvst` | Enable Rapid PVST+ (Cisco's RSTP implementation) globally |
| `spanning-tree mode mst` | Enable MSTP instead (not covered in this video, but the other "rapid" option) |
| `show spanning-tree [vlan <id>]` | Show root bridge, port roles/states, priorities, per VLAN |
| `show spanning-tree summary` | Quick summary of mode and root status per VLAN |
| `show spanning-tree interface <intf>` | Role/state for a specific interface |
| `spanning-tree link-type point-to-point` | Manually force a port's link type (normally auto-detected from duplex) |
| `spanning-tree link-type shared` | Manually force shared link type (disables rapid transition on that port) |
| `spanning-tree portfast` (interface) | Mark a port as an Edge Port (host-facing) |
| `spanning-tree portfast bpduguard default` | Auto shut down any edge/PortFast port that receives a BPDU |
| `debug spanning-tree events` | Real-time view of role/state transitions (lab/troubleshooting use) |

In `show spanning-tree` output, roles are typically abbreviated:
- `Root` — Root Port
- `Desg` — Designated Port
- `Altn` — Alternate Port
- `Back` — Backup Port

And states appear abbreviated too:
- `FWD` — Forwarding
- `LRN` — Learning
- `BLK` — Discarding (still often displayed/labeled as "blocking" in Cisco CLI output for familiarity, even though internally it's the RSTP "discarding" state)

